Say what a string measured, and what rect it was drawn in.

NSStringDrawer had a trace on one of its four paths: CIDER_TRACE_TEXT prints CIDER_TEXTSIZE for
sizeOfAttributedString:, added when a used rect one line short was clipping wizard text. The plain
string size and both draws had nothing.

That gap cost a wrong conclusion within the hour it was found. Money Manager Ex draws a weekday
label as Wednesda, eight complete glyphs and then blank space, and the obvious suspect was our own
string measurement answering short. Tracing sizeOfString: showed 53 measurements and no weekday in
them, which reads as "not measured here" and is only worth believing because the same trace proves
it can speak at all.

WHAT THE THREE TRACES TOGETHER ESTABLISH, on one drive of the New Transaction dialog:

    CIDER_MEASURE        53 calls, all digits and menu titles
    CIDER_TEXTSIZE       39 calls, and one of them is len=9 answering used=65.00x14.00
    CIDER_MEASURE draw   51 calls, all title bar and menu bar

Wednesday is nine characters and 65 points is right for it: the eight glyphs actually drawn occupy
about 58 in the capture, and the ninth needs about seven more. SO THE MEASUREMENT IS CORRECT AND
THE DEFECT IS NOT HERE. wx draws that label by a route none of these four paths covers, and the
next person chasing it should start from that rather than from our text measurement, which is where
I started and lost a drive to.

CIDER_TRACE_MEASURE, off by default, one getenv per call on paths that already build a layout
manager and run it.

